{
  "id": "Compound::DB00327 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Hydromorphone's relationship with Cyp3a4 is supported by multiple pathways that converge through the opioid receptor agonist and organic heteropentacyclic compound classes. The evidence suggests that Hydromorphone, through its inclusion in the Full Opioid Agonists category, binds to Cyp3a4 via Alfentanil, a member of this group. This binding mechanism is further reinforced by the shared ancestry of Hydromorphone and Alfentanil with the Opioid Receptor Agonist and Organic Heteropentacyclic Compound classes. Additionally, Hydromorphone's ability to cause Breakthrough Pain and Cheyne-Stokes Respiration, both of which are associated with Morphine, which in turn binds to Cyp3a4, further supports a link between Hydromorphone and Cyp3a4. The recurring involvement of opioid receptor agonists and the shared structural features in these pathways highlight a potential mechanism involving enzyme induction or direct interaction with Cyp3a4. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, suggesting a robust relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
